  "labelled": [
    {
      "task": "TASK-110",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-9A47DF868BD4, TASK-AC-2E6734369AC5",
      "text": "BlockPanel takes `detailLine`: the badge names the format alone and the block's size it leaves out (rounds, scheme) is read once, on a `clr-timed-meta` line directly under the header (the line Review and the timed flow already draw). Only the circuit asks for it."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-110",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-2E6734369AC5, TASK-AC-9A47DF868BD4",
      "text": "The circuit's badge is format-only (`CIRCUIT`, was `CIRCUIT · 3 ROUNDS` outside the product presentation) and its prescribed rounds (`3 ROUNDS`) are read on the line under the header; under the product presentation Round 7 had dropped the rounds from the card before a round was recorded. The circuit-round state's card gains that one line."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-110",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-4BEA11242321, AC-R003-03, TASK-AC-9A47DF868BD4",
      "text": "Each live row's name, compact equipment and prescribed load are `liveMovementReadings` (the load-guidance read model's target through `loadText`), drawn exactly as before. The prescription line carries `data-structure-meta` and, for an EMOM with a rest window, `Ns rest at the end of each minute` after its window; the cards state's EMOM prescribes no rest, so its line is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-110",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-4BEA11242321",
      "text": "The live ladder's summary line reads its name and load through `liveMovementReadings`, drawn exactly as before. Not in a state compared here."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-110",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-2E6734369AC5",
      "text": "SectionHeader's full (non-compact) structure list names each block by its format alone (`StructureBadge formatOnly`). The route and the accepted gallery draw the compact navigator, which has no list; the registry's full-header specimen holds no blocks, so nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "AC-R008-02",
      "text": "Every urgent timer and the one aura share one warning loop and one phase: each urgent clock claims the view's one urgent loop, every urgent timer breathes while any claim runs (bec4454 stilled a second urgent timer), the first draws the one edge, and each new breathe is pinned to the document timeline's epoch. Fed by each clock's deadline adapter."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "AC-R008-01",
      "text": "The urgent timer breathes on the edge's own rule — the same keyframes, 1.5 s period and easing (.2/.8/.2), a steady .5 when still or under reduced motion — in place of the shipped four-second stepped micro-pulse on the timer. The urgency state's urgent clock breathes with its edge; under reduced motion both hold .5."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-ED9D1944F3CE",
      "text": "TimerFrame carries the breathe on its `role=\"timer\"` element (`clr-countdown-breathe`, `data-urgent`, the warning loop) in place of `clr-pulse-micro` on its wrapper; CountdownBar and RestTimerBar read the rest's deadline (`restDeadline`): the low colour, the fill's colour and \"Final 10 seconds\" from ten seconds, the breathe on the rest's timer (not the card) and the edge from five."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-A5D62CC0272B",
      "text": "The compact SectionHeader reads \"Section N / M · status\" to assistive technology, visually hidden, and its visible \"N / M\" is decoration of the trigger (`aria-hidden`), so the trigger's one name is \"All sections\". Nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-ED9D1944F3CE",
      "text": "Each format clock's warning reads its adapter (EMOM minute, AMRAP window, race cap): held while paused, none once ended. The low colour at ten and the edge at five are as before; the breathe is the change above."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-23D0ADE293F8",
      "text": "The circuit's round rest is one whole TimerFrame (the app's Card in the timer role) fed by `circuitRestDeadline`, in place of the package's TimerDisplay whose stepped micro-pulse ran through the last ten seconds. No state compared here draws a circuit; the circuit-round state shows it in the same commit."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-23D0ADE293F8",
      "text": "A scheduled ladder's interval countdown is one whole TimerFrame fed by `scheduleIntervalDeadline`. No accepted state draws a schedule."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-ED9D1944F3CE",
      "text": "The movement countdown reads `movementCountdownDeadline`; its warning is unchanged but for the breathe above."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-ED9D1944F3CE",
      "text": "CountdownDisplay takes an optional deadline from its consumer; its drawing is unchanged (the route no longer draws it)."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-ED9D1944F3CE",
      "text": "The adapters read only the fields of a view they need, so the route's flow feeds its attempt through them. Nothing drawn changes."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-DCFC4C79B85A",
      "text": "Previous, Next and a jump move focus to the opened section's first card with a temporary tabindex, falling back to its heading. Not a gallery state."
    },
    {
      "task": "TASK-108",
      "criterion": "TASK-AC-8E1E91D4F4AA",
      "text": "TASK-007's one-row header: the cluster never wraps to a second line; the title gives up width first and, at 23.75rem and below, takes the h3 size on the same line height. No accepted state draws the workout header."
    }
  ],
  "unintended": []
}
